{"uid":"9dd279875078048d","name":"test_an_uncorroborated_no_verdict_now_backs_off_instead_of_tripping_the_three_strike_guard","fullName":"tests.test_progress_budget_task013#test_an_uncorroborated_no_verdict_now_backs_off_instead_of_tripping_the_three_strike_guard","historyId":"14224bd620a8aacb977d07633a596204","time":{"start":1792161019175,"stop":1792161019266,"duration":91},"description":"Three consecutive iterations, each claiming `commit` evidence but\n    touching NOTHING in the workspace -- `_apply_worker_progress_report`\n    reads this as uncorroborated every time (task 012's own pinned\n    behaviour, `test_commit_evidence_with_no_tree_delta_is_not_corroborated`).\n\n    This test used to prove requirement A.3's letter (\"keeps today's\n    three-strike witness rule\") held unchanged. PRD v0.29 #279 (task 014's\n    sweep cure) supersedes it for exactly this shape: #279's own\n    `_apply_engine_repoll_backoff` trigger is defined over the SAME signal\n    (`verdict == \"no_verdict\"`, `corroborated: false`, `deltaSize: 0`, two\n    consecutive times on one task), and it intercepts BEFORE a third such\n    pass can ever reach the three-strike guard's own counter -- pass 2 is\n    the first ordinary witness (old counter -> 1) and simultaneously the\n    first of what becomes two consecutive re-polls, so pass 3 backs the\n    task off for 600s instead of becoming the guard's third witness\n    (requirement A.3's own \"a re-poll that triggers a backoff neither\n    increments nor resets the approach's stagnation counter\"). task 014's\n    own sweep crashed an xdist worker on this exact node before this cure\n    -- this module's `_worker_sup` built `sup` directly rather than through\n    `tests.conftest.make_supervisor`, leaving the backoff's real\n    `asyncio.sleep(600)` unpatched (`_patch_sleep_for_this_test()` now\n    closes that, matching `tests/test_repoll_backoff.py`'s own documented\n    reasoning for the same gap).\n\n    What is left to pin, and what this rewrite asserts instead: the claims\n    are still recorded and still uncorroborated every time (task 012's\n    letter, unaffected by #279); the OLD three-strike message never\n    appears (superseded, not merely absent by accident); #279's own\n    backoff fires twice (`consecutiveCount` 2 then 3, since the third\n    scripted call is ALSO a re-poll on the already-once-backed-off task);\n    and the task ends up deferred (`pending`, a `re-poll backoff`\n    `deferredReason`).","descriptionHtml":"<p>Three consecutive iterations, each claiming <code>commit</code> evidence but<br />\ntouching NOTHING in the workspace -- <code>_apply_worker_progress_report</code><br />\nreads this as uncorroborated every time (task 012's own pinned<br />\nbehaviour, <code>test_commit_evidence_with_no_tree_delta_is_not_corroborated</code>).</p>\n<pre><code>This test used to prove requirement A.3's letter (&quot;keeps today's\nthree-strike witness rule&quot;) held unchanged. PRD v0.29 #279 (task 014's\nsweep cure) supersedes it for exactly this shape: #279's own\n`_apply_engine_repoll_backoff` trigger is defined over the SAME signal\n(`verdict == &quot;no_verdict&quot;`, `corroborated: false`, `deltaSize: 0`, two\nconsecutive times on one task), and it intercepts BEFORE a third such\npass can ever reach the three-strike guard's own counter -- pass 2 is\nthe first ordinary witness (old counter -&gt; 1) and simultaneously the\nfirst of what becomes two consecutive re-polls, so pass 3 backs the\ntask off for 600s instead of becoming the guard's third witness\n(requirement A.3's own &quot;a re-poll that triggers a backoff neither\nincrements nor resets the approach's stagnation counter&quot;). task 014's\nown sweep crashed an xdist worker on this exact node before this cure\n-- this module's `_worker_sup` built `sup` directly rather than through\n`tests.conftest.make_supervisor`, leaving the backoff's real\n`asyncio.sleep(600)` unpatched (`_patch_sleep_for_this_test()` now\ncloses that, matching `tests/test_repoll_backoff.py`'s own documented\nreasoning for the same gap).\n\nWhat is left to pin, and what this rewrite asserts instead: the claims\nare still recorded and still uncorroborated every time (task 012's\nletter, unaffected by #279); the OLD three-strike message never\nappears (superseded, not merely absent by accident); #279's own\nbackoff fires twice (`consecutiveCount` 2 then 3, since the third\nscripted call is ALSO a re-poll on the already-once-backed-off task);\nand the task ends up deferred (`pending`, a `re-poll backoff`\n`deferredReason`).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1792160405917,"stop":1792160405917,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792160405917,"stop":1792160405917,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1792161019127,"stop":1792161019127,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1792161019128,"stop":1792161019149,"duration":21},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1792161019149,"stop":1792161019149,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage